# Overlay: LVGL refresh period 10 ms instead of the 33 ms default.
#
# Build with:
#   idf.py -B build-refr10 -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.refr10" build
#
# Why this is a separate measurement rather than a setting: the default caps
# LVGL at 30.3 Hz while this panel scans at 37.8 Hz, and the two rates beat
# against each other. Every rendered frame is then held for either one or two
# panel refreshes in an irregular pattern, which is invisible on a changing
# digit and obvious on continuously moving content — the §7.5 marquee label is
# the most sensitive thing on the screen. The measurement above the fold is that
# the frame interval sits at exactly 33 001 us: the frame rate is set by this
# constant, not by how long a frame takes to draw.
#
# 10 ms rather than 26 ms (the panel period): LVGL's refresh timer is not phase
# locked to VSYNC, so asking for exactly one frame per refresh still lands
# wherever the two clocks happen to be. Rendering faster than the panel scans
# lets every scan-out pick up the most recent content instead.
CONFIG_LV_DEF_REFR_PERIOD=10
